<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Breath Weapons</h1>
<p>Dragons and other great monsters breathe their attacks. Each breath strikes 
everyone in the room at once, except the monster's own group, and gods 
who are invisible. Beginners up to level 20 are never hit by a breath.
</p>
<ul><li><b>fire breath</b> (Fire sphere): a blast of flame; less against chain and plate</li>
<li><b>frost breath</b> (Frost sphere): a freezing blast</li>
<li><b>lightning breath</b> (Electricity sphere): bolts of lightning; a shield is no use</li>
<li><b>acid breath</b> (Acid sphere): a spray of acid</li>
<li><b>gas breath</b> (Poison sphere): a choking cloud; terrible against light armour, much weaker against plate; a shield is no use</li>
<li><b>light breath</b> (Mind sphere): a blast of dazzling colours</li>
<li><b>shard breath</b> (Summoning sphere): a storm of sharp shards</li>
<li><b>sonic breath</b> (Mind sphere): a shattering roar, strongest against plate; a shield is no use</li></ul>
<p>Except where the list says otherwise, a shield softens the blow. To 
withstand a breath, raise the sphere it belongs to: the resistance spells 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Heat Resistance</a>) help against the matching breath, and so does 
your own skill in that sphere (see <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>).
</p><p>No guild teaches the breaths, and they don't come in random treasure. 
Only the greater monsters breathe the true breath: a lesser monster's 
fire, frost, lightning, acid, gas or light breath comes out as the 
matching spell instead (a fireball, frostball, lightning bolt, acid ball, 
stinking cloud or colour spray), weaker the lower its level.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
